+META GAMING now has two isolated, read-only catalogue profiles for the Normal
+MYR and Free Credit MYR accounts. Their gateway paths, cache keys, catalogue
+account labels and player/ledger namespaces are separate. Both profiles remain
+`adapter_unimplemented` and `playable=false`; this release does not enable a
+launch, balance, transfer, settlement or recovery route. Remote META artwork is
+not trusted until the supplier confirms an official image host, so the portal
+uses the local provider artwork.
 
 JILI now has a legacy transfer protocol, executable adapter, per-account runtime factory and the universal game-wallet API. Its 1:1 and 1:100 catalogues have separate cache keys and check the account, currency and ratio. Deposits are confirmed by querying the original account, transaction, direction and normalized amount. Returns use the supplier's all-funds transfer rather than a delayed balance. A zero return still needs a real supplier receipt. Unknown transfers remain reserved; recovery never resubmits them.
 
