+# MASTER7 META GAMING catalogue candidate
+
+Date: 2026-11-10
+Baseline: `17.0.0-selfbuilt.148-jili-transfer-wallet`
+State: local candidate only; not deployed
+
+## Scope
+
+This candidate adds two independent, read-only META GAMING catalogue profiles:
+
+| Portal profile | Gateway request | Portal balance class | Runtime adapter |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| `metagaming_normal_myr` | `GET /providers/metagaming/games?account=normal` | `cash` | `adapter_unimplemented` |
+| `metagaming_free_myr` | `GET /providers/metagaming/games?account=free` | `free_credit` | `adapter_unimplemented` |
+
+The profiles have separate player namespaces, ledger namespaces and catalogue
+cache keys. A successful normalized gateway response must identify the exact
+`provider`, `account` and `currency` expected by the requested profile:
+
+```json
+{
+  "provider": "metagaming",
+  "account": "normal",
+  "currency": "MYR",
+  "games": []
+}
+```
+
+Any metadata mismatch blocks the refresh and retains the previous snapshot in
+maintenance state. Catalogue rows are always returned with `playable=false`.
+There is no launch, wallet, transfer, settlement or recovery implementation in
+this candidate, and neither profile can perform a funds operation.
+
+## Artwork policy
+
+The official META GAMING integration document describes `ImageUrl` and shows
+only the template `https://<base-domain-url>/thumbs/Web/<GameCode>.png`. It
+does not identify a concrete production thumbnail hostname. Remote META image
+URLs are therefore rejected. Catalogue rows use the existing local
+`/assets/providers/metagaming.webp` fallback until an official host or asset
+manifest is supplied and reviewed.
+
+## Legacy MegaH5 boundary
+
+The existing `megah5` catalogue and `megah5_myr` profile are unchanged. The
+available META GAMING document and credential attachment names do not prove
+that legacy MegaH5 is the same merchant account or protocol. Renaming,
+relabelling, enabling, or sharing a cache/player/ledger namespace would create
+an unsafe mapping. Legacy MegaH5 therefore remains separate and fail-closed
+under the existing production controls while its mapping remains ambiguous.
+
+## Evidence boundary
+
+Implementation used only the supplied offline META GAMING document and
+existing repository artwork. No provider endpoint was called, no credential or
+secret was added, and no deployment or environment configuration was changed.
+This is catalogue contract work, not production provider acceptance.
